# env

Bionic toolchain for AGY: a self-contained Android prefix installed at
`$PREFIX` (`/data/data/com.agy/files/usr`), a package manager (`pkg`), and a
path-rewrite helper. No root, no proot.

```
env/bootstrap/   Termux bootstrap archive + prefix patch
env/overlay/     files copied verbatim into $PREFIX (etc, bin/rish, ...)
env/pkg/         pkg + its shell libraries
env/dist/env/    packaged assets consumed by EnvInstaller
env/tests/       offline selftest / invariant / e3 checks
```

## Termux prefix rewriting

The Termux bootstrap and its packages are compiled with
`/data/data/com.termux/files/usr` hardcoded: in shebangs, in helper bodies
(`gzexe` tmpdir, dpkg `.list`, `*-config`), and in absolute symlinks. Our
prefix is different, so every occurrence must be repointed.

Two layers do this:

1. **Install time.** `EnvInstaller.rewriteTermuxPrefixes(prefix)` walks text
   files under `$PREFIX/{bin,libexec,etc,share,var}` and replaces every
   `/data/data/com.<anyid>/files/usr` with `$PREFIX` (atomic in-place rewrite;
   binary/ELF files and symlinks skipped). `pkg install` does the same for each
   package right after extraction, via `rewrite_prefix` in `pkg/lib/util.sh`.
2. **After third-party installers.** `pip`, `npm` and friends write console
   scripts that bake in the Termux interpreter path. Run the shipped helper:

```sh
agy-fix-paths                 # rewrite the whole prefix
agy-fix-paths ~/site/bin      # only these files/dirs
agy-fix-paths ./venv/bin/*    # globs expanded by the shell
```

`agy-fix-paths` prints the number of files rewritten. It is idempotent (files
already using `$PREFIX` are left byte-identical) and skips binaries and
symlinks. It lives at `env/overlay/bin/agy-fix-paths` and is installed to
`$PREFIX/bin/agy-fix-paths`.
